28 0 obj
<<
/Title (The biggest lesson from this lab was simple: Build it, then catch it. The simulation showed me what the attack looked like from the GoPhish side. Splunk showed me what it looked like from the defender side. Every control mapped to something I actually observed: Spam filtering. Remote image blocking. URL sandboxing. MFA. Scheduled detection. Both sides of initial access, built safely, then detected. Full writeup and SPL detections are on GitHub. #ERSec)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 127 0 R
>>
endobj
